# The worker's build context is the repository root. The build stage installs
# the workspace from its lockfile and bundles the worker from it, and only the
# bundle, Playwright and Chromium reach the image (see the Dockerfile). These
# stay out of the context altogether, so they are never sent to a builder:
# anything that can hold a secret, agents' and tools' own files, and what is
# large and unused.
#
# Both builders read this file. BuildKit takes a `<Dockerfile>.dockerignore`
# beside the Dockerfile, and flyctl takes fly.toml's `ignorefile`, resolved
# beside fly.toml. A flyctl that finds no ignore file sends everything.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
.git
.github
.claude
.agents
.dashboard
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.cache
**/.turbo
**/dist
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
apps/web/preview
docs
supabase
